title: Per-file transcripts + media preview split-pane with click-to-seek
summary: 'Closed the multi-media transcript-association gap surfaced during v1 UX testing. New `transcribe-orchestrator.ts` exposes `transcribeMediaFile(projectDir, basename, opts)` which wraps the legacy `transcribeProject` and mirrors the result to `<projectDir>/transcripts/<basename>.json` (per-file canonical location). The legacy single-source `transcript.json` continues to be written for back-compat. Updated `listMediaFiles`/`hasTranscript` to check both root and per-file paths; `buildProjectTranscripts` enumerates both. Sidebar in workspace-app.ts subscribes to `media:list:changed`/`transcript:added` WS envelopes for live refresh after ingest. MediaPreview gained a split-pane layout: when the selected media has a transcript, video/audio renders left + per-word clickable transcript renders right with click-to-seek behavior + currently-playing word highlight (atel-transcript-word--current). 323 tests passing (+7 new), compliance clean.'
